SUMMARY: Flashback (X Avant XXI: Memory Mannnnn\, Night 2)
DESCRIPTION:Sonic Bikes improvises with the soundworld of bicycles\, and 
 Bilal Nasser’s a punk & post-rock infused set delves into resistance\, co
 mmemoration\, and lament.\n\nIn the first set\, local artist Stephanie Or
 lando brings her Sonic Bikes to the stage. A bespoke ensemble of improvis
 ing percussionists will make use of reassembled and sonified bike parts t
 o animate a familiar soundworld of gears\, spokes\, and pedals. The perfo
 rmance takes on added weight as each artist exerts and sustains a particu
 lar pedal-powered labour to realize the piece\, which is found in their c
 onstantly negotiated collective space.\n\nDuring each of the other nights
  of the festival\, Stephanie’s sound sculptures will be set up in the ven
 ue for audiences to interact and improvise with.\n\nDuring the second set
 \, Bilal Nasser will perform delay- and reverb-drenched solo works for gu
 itar and voice. He will also be joined by a chamber ensemble to present a
  genre-bending suite about genocidal crisis and diasporic despair. Bilal 
 blends post-rock\, post-classical\, punk\, electronic\, and shoegaze in a
  musical statement of commemoration\, resistance\, healing and lament. Th
 is performance marks the Toronto launch of Bilal’s album\, Every Martyr i
 s a Universe\, on Constellation Records.\n\nAll prices are inclusive of H
 ST.
CATEGORIES:Concert,First-Unitarian-Church
X-TKF-FEATURED-IMAGE:https://d3flpus5evl89n.cloudfront.net/6755f3e6a02aaf
 1c2599e757/6ab3359ecd7aa68c2cae2665/scaled_1024.jpg
