SUMMARY: Ancient Circuitry (X Avant XXI: Memory Mannnnn\, Night 3)
DESCRIPTION:Gathering two artist’s projects in concert form\, Ancient Cir
 cuitry combines Mani Mazinani’s Solar Organ and Alexis Nanibush-Pamajewon
 g’s For The Youth: Reilluminated\, connecting with ancestral knowledge to
 day.\n\nSolar Organ Ensemble moves between improvised and composed music 
 using traditional and invented pentatonic scales covering a spectrum of a
 pproaches to pentatonic sound generation. Solar Organ https://manimazinan
 i.net/project.html?project=Solar-Organ \, an electronic pentatonic instru
 ment created by Mani Mazinani\, connects neurobiology with the geographic
  and historic ubiquity of pentatonic practice\, a universal human phenome
 non.\n\nFor The Youth: Reilluminated by Alexis Nanibush-Pamajewong\, is a
  re-creation of a light and sound installation https://www.instagram.com/
 alexisnanibush_pamaj/p/DQngD8REaYa/?img_index=2 with local Indigenous you
 th performances — to honour the life\, kinship\, and the spirit of genera
 tions past\, present\, and future.\n\nCurated by Mani Mazinani\n\nINSTALL
 ATION\nOutside of performances\, attendees can interact with sound sculpt
 ures from Night 2 https://musicgallery.org/events/flashback/ artist Steph
 anie Orlando.\n\nInspired by everyday sounds from her time working as a b
 ike mechanic\, Stephanie Orlando’s Sonic Bikes installation invites atten
 dees to interact with the spectrum of noises and musical textures of recy
 cled bike parts.\n\nAll prices are inclusive of HST.
CATEGORIES:Concert,First-Unitarian-Church
