URL:https://tockify.com/torevent/detail/24357/1792861200000
SUMMARY: CLOSING RECEPTION of VENUS VS PINK Exhibition presented by Susan
  N Stewart and Catharina Goldnau
DESCRIPTION:VENUS VS PINK EXHIBITION\n\nTwo artists. Two very different w
 orlds. One seriously colourful encounter.\n\nSusan N Stewart brings the h
 eat with bold\, vibrant paintings that swing from pure joy and excitement
  to moments of unexpected calm and serenity.\n\nCatharina Goldnau's VENUS
  sculptures are a different kind of force. Each figure is hand-crafted fr
 om custom clay\, capturing a distinct emotional state — raw\, imperfect\,
  powerful\, and unapologetically human. And holding it all together?\nA s
 olid foundation of Canadian Shield rock.\n\n\nPaint meets clay. Colour me
 ets earth. Pink meets Venus.\n\nCome see what happens when these worlds c
 ollide at the Dignam Gallery in the Women's Art Association of Canada! Ta
 lk to the incredible artists and enjoy the beautiful space with refreshme
 nts on Saturday October 24th\, 2026 from 1-4PM.\n\n\nARTIST STATEMENTS\n\
 nSusan N Stewart\n\n"PINK PUTS UP A FIGHT"\n\nAfter two months of artisti
 c combat and a mounting body count of discarded paintings\, I was ambushe
 d by PINK.\n\nPINK was everything I distrusted: frivolous\, girlish\, che
 erful and entirely lacking in gravitas.\n\nI attacked with brushes\, scra
 pers and considerable indignation. PINK retaliated with MAGENTA.\n\nThe b
 attle was ugly. The casualties were numerous.\n\nThen something unexpecte
 d happened. I finally began to like my paintings.\n\nPINK has since retai
 ned legal counsel and is demanding full credit.\n\n\nCatharina Goldnau\n\
 nAt the heart of my sculptural practice is femininity in all its messy\, 
 magnificent complexity. My Venuses aren’t here to pose\, please\, or conf
 orm. They are raw\, imperfect\, sensual\, vulnerable\, and strong — bodie
 s that carry stories\, contradictions\, and the marks of being human.\n\n
 As a mother of two daughters and grandmother to five girls\, I’m deeply i
 nvested in how we experience girlhood and womanhood\, both physically and
  psychologically. I draw on lived experience\, observation\, and intuitio
 n to create figures that challenge the polished ideals imposed on the fem
 ale body.\n\nI’m interested in what happens when we stop trying to fix\, 
 flatten\, or idealize women — and start seeing them as they are. My work 
 is an invitation to question who gets to define beauty\, to embrace imper
 fection\, and to claim the freedom to inhabit our bodies on our own terms
 .
CATEGORIES:Art-Show/Gallery-Event,Dignam-Gallery
