SUMMARY: Brownman's HALLOWEEN THRILLER (MJ as electric-jazz) - Toronto en
 d-of-tour party!
DESCRIPTION:HALLOWEEN THRILLER 2026 :: www.Thriller.Brownman.com http://w
 ww.Thriller.Brownman.com\nTIX: www.eventbrite.ca/e/2001549304851 http://w
 ww.eventbrite.ca/e/2001549304851\n----\nJUNO & GRAMMY nominated jazz/hip-
 hop trumpet playing iconoclast BROWNMAN ALI (Jay-z\, Missy Elliot\, Kanye
  West\, Guru's Jazzmatazz) will once again lead an all-star quartet throu
 gh his popular annual HALLOWEEN THRILLER concert\, this year travelling u
 p from Brooklyn\, NY to various venues (and schools) across Southern Onta
 rio. The much lauded BROWNMAN ELECTRYC TRIO + 1 will perform the entire M
 ichael Jackson "Thriller" recording\, interpreted and re-worked in the Mi
 les Davis-esque fashion this multiple National Jazz Award winning improvi
 ser has become known for. In addition to the quartet performing Thriller 
 from top to bottom\, other MJ classics will be featured through the night
  for this unique Halloween Series jazz party. Costumes and Thriller video
  dance moves encouraged!\n\n[ TICKETS: http://www.eventbrite.ca/e/2001549
 304851 ]\n\nThis show features as it's "+1" acclaimed keyboardist NICK MA
 CLEAN -- a JUNO Award nominee\, a signee to Brownman's Browntasauras Reco
 rds label & winner of 10 Global Music Awards -- standing alongside 2 of T
 oronto's most in demand musicians : SEAN DENNIS on 6-string electric bass
  (called "a once in a generation bass player" by the Head of the Humber C
 ollege Bass Department when he was a student there)\, and ADAM MANSFIELD 
 on drums (25-year old drumset phenom)\, all under the direction of 2x Nat
 ional Jazz Award winning modern jazz trumpet iconoclast BROWNMAN ALI. Ple
 ase visit http://www.Thriller.Brownman.com for more info on this year's H
 alloween Thriller Series.\n\n"Delving so deeply into that record always l
 eaves us speechless"\, states Ali. "Michael birthed so many incredible tu
 nes over the years\, but his collaborations with Quincy Jones on Thriller
  has to be one of the most towering musical achievements in pop music eve
 r. Using that brilliant material every year on Halloween\, as jump-offs f
 or what we do makes for a party that's both danceable\, but still rooted 
 in exploratory improvising and deep reaching solos. We approach it the wa
 y Miles might have."\n\nThe BROWNMAN ELECTRYC TRIO has won a National Jaz
 z Award\, 3 Toronto Independent Music Awards\, a SOCAN music award\, a CB
 C Galaxie Rising Star Award\, and an International Independent Music Awar
 d for "Jazz-Funk album of the year" for their latest release "Gravitation
 "\, which hit number 4 on the iTunes USA jazz charts upon it's release.\n
 \n“Awards are nice\, naturally\, but to dig what Brownman is doing\, you’
 ve got to see him live. I had a chance to do just that over the summer wh
 en Brownman fronted his killer trio ... I came away with a blown mind. Th
 is guy’s got chops galore\, soul to match\, and a sense of phrasing that 
 recalls many of the greats\, but suggests itself to be his own.”\n-- The 
 Buffalo News on the latest slew of awards for the Brownman Electryc Trio\
 n\n----\n\nSat-Oct-31 -- TORONTO\n@ My House\n2882 Dundas St. W.\, Toront
 o\, ON\, M6P 1Y8\n http://www.MyHouseInTheJunction.com\n\n7:00pm -- doors
 \n8:00pm -- show\n$25 -- advance (with costume)\n$30 -- advance (no costu
 me)\n$20 -- students / arts worker\nTIX: http://www.eventbrite.ca/e/20015
 49304851\n$35 -- at-the-door on show-night (if space available)\n\n----\n
 *** 1st come\, 1st serve for seating\, so arrive early to ensure an optim
 al sight-line (as front of house seats have the best sight-lines).\n----\
 nConsider a dinner reservation -- check out My House's award-winning menu
 :\nmyhouseinthejunction.com/menu https://myhouseinthejunction.com/menu\n-
 ---\n\n2026 HALLOWEEN THRILLER -- ONT. TOUR DATES\nwww.Thriller.Brownman.
 com http://www.Thriller.Brownman.com\nMon-Oct-21\, day : TORONTO -- schoo
 l masterclass\nTue-Oct-20\, 7pm : COURTICE @ Sir Monty's\nWed-Oct-21\, 7p
 m : KINGSTON @ RCHA Club\nThr-Oct-22\, 7pm : WESTPORT @ Cove Inn\nFri-Oct
 -23\, 7pm : MONTREAL @ Upstairs Jazz\nSat-Oct-24\, 7pm : OTTAWA @ Night O
 at\nSun-Oct-25\, 7pm : travel day\nMon-Oct-26\, day : TORONTO -- school m
 asterclass\nTue-Oct-27\, 7pm : NEWMARKET @ George Whiskey Lounge\nWed-Oct
 -28\, 7pm : BARRIE @ Tequilazzo\nThr-Oct-29\, 7pm : KITCHENER @ Arabella 
 Park Beer Bar\nFri-Oct-30\, 8pm : HAMILTON @ Henry's On James\nSat-Oct-31
 \, 8pm : TORONTO @ My House\n\n----\n\n:: Brownman Ali - electric trumpet
  & spookiness\n--> http://www.Brownman.com\n:: Nick Maclean - keyboards &
  ghoulishness\n--> http://www.NickMacleanJazz.com\n:: Sean Dennis - elect
 ric bass & creepiness\n--> http://www.Instagram.com/seanydmusic\n:: Adam 
 Mansfield - drums & ghastliness\n--> http://www.Instagram.com/adammansfie
 ld8\n\n----\nDress up if you like - it's Halloween!!!\n----\n\nSee videos
  from the 2020 HALLOWEEN THRILLER show:\n http://www.youtube.com/playlist
 ?list=PLFEa9tcDLHdLgeCGMKT5BfiWAv7IGymNv\n\n\nHear the BROWNMAN ELECTRYC 
 TRIO at:\n http://www.ElectrycTrio.Brownman.com\n\n\nVideos of BROWNMAN E
 LECTRYC TRIO live:\n http://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLFECA3E452FE2B
 C0D\n\n\n----\nABOUT BROWNMAN | http://www.Brownman.com\n----\nHeralded a
 s “Canada’s preeminent Jazz trumpeter” by NYC’s Village Voice\, Brownman 
 Ali - born on the small Caribbean island of Trinidad\, & schooled in NYC 
 - is a multiple award-winning NYC-schooled protégé to his teacher\, Gramm
 y-winning trumpet legend\, Randy Brecker. Splitting his time between Toro
 nto and New York\, he tirelessly leads 8 unique ensembles of his own incl
 uding the internationally acclaimed Miles Davis influenced BROWNMAN ELECT
 RYC TRIO\, and the award-winning CRUZAO latin-jazz quintet. All these ens
 embles record under Brownman's own much lauded BROWNTASAURAS RECORDS labe
 l\, established in 2009. In high demand in the studio world with over 300
  CD appearances to date\, Brownman delivers stylistically authentic horn 
 playing over a wide range of styles from bebop to hiphop having worked wi
 th the likes of Guru's Jazzmatazz (replacing Donald Byrd in that primordi
 al ensemble)\, Mos Def\, KRS-1\, Quincy Jones\, Paul Simon\, Jay-z\, Miss
 y Elliot\, Mingus Dynasty Big Band\, Gary Bartz\, Chucho Valdes & far too
  many more to name here. He is considered to be one of the most unique an
 d provocative improvising trumpet players in the nation today and is wide
 ly regarded as a vanguard for the evolution of Jazz in Canada.\n\n"One of
  the next great voices in the new generation of jazz improvisers”\n-- Ran
 dy Brecker\n\n----\nAWARDS & ACCOLADES\n----\nA highly decorated player\,
  his awards & accolades include :\n-- multiple JUNO Award nominations\n--
  GRAMMY Award long-listed (w/ Brownman Electryc Trio)\n-- 2 National Jazz
  Awards (with 11 nominations over the years)\n-- 10 Global Music Awards\n
 -- winner of the International Song Competition (ISC) - Jazz Category\n--
  Montreal Jazz Fest's "Grand Prix Du Jazz" award\n-- a CBC Galaxie Rising
  Star award\n-- a SOCAN composers award\n-- an International Independent 
 Music Award for "Album of the Year"\n-- 7 Toronto Independent Music Award
  "jazz artist of the year" (11 nominations)\n-- a Black IMPACT Award for 
 "Musician of the Year"\n-- a Black Canadian Award nomination for "Jazz Mu
 sician of the Year"\n-- an induction into the WHO'S WHO IN BLACK CANADA\n
 -- a Caribbean Music & Entertainment nomination for "Jazz Artist of the Y
 ear"\n-- a BRAVO! channel documentary on his life\n-- NOW magazine naming
  him "Toronto's Best Jazz Musician"\n-- CBC Radio Canada named him "one o
 f the most recorded trumpet players in Canadian history"\n-- NPR in New Y
 ork calls him "the new standard in electric jazz"\n-- the Trinidad & Toba
 go Consulate General awarded him with a citation for being a "Distinguish
 ed National of Trinidad"\n-- was once listed by Air Canada's in-flight ma
 gazine as "One of the Top 10 reasons to visit Toronto".
CATEGORIES:Concert,My-House
