SUMMARY: WORLD PREMIERE – “The Art of Lockdown”
DESCRIPTION:The year is 2020. The world as we know it has changed forever
 . Artists whose lives and livelihoods depended on bringing people togethe
 r were faced with a terrifying question:\n\n“What do we do now?”\n\nIntro
 ducing The Art of Lockdown\, a five-episode documentary series exploring 
 the impact of the COVID-19 pandemic on the arts and entertainment industr
 y.\n\nEach episode delves into the life and journey of a different artist
 \, revealing how they navigated the uncertainty\, challenges\, and unprec
 edented changes brought on by the pandemic. From a one-woman clown show t
 o a black and white murder mystery\, every artist has a story to tell!\n\
 nJoin us at Fox Theatre on November 5th at 7:30pm for the world premiere 
 of this compelling new series.\n\nStick around after the screening to con
 nect with fellow Toronto artists\, meet the filmmakers\, and take part in
  a Q&A Session for a behind-the-scenes look at the making of the series.\
 n\n\nTickets: www.tickettailor.com/events/blackalloyproductions/2340506 h
 ttps://www.tickettailor.com/events/blackalloyproductions/2340506\n\n\n‘Th
 e Art of Lockdown’ is a timely exploration about artistic resilience\, cr
 eativity\, and perseverance in the face of overwhelming odds. It shines a
  light on the people who create the stories we love and highlights the de
 termination it takes to keep creating\, even when the world came to a sta
 ndstill.\n\nAcross five episodes\, The Art of Lockdown explores the creat
 ivity\, resilience\, and reinvention of artists navigating an unprecedent
 ed moment in history. From experimental filmmaking to personal accounts o
 f an industry in crisis\, each episode offers a unique perspective on the
  pandemic’s impact on the arts.\n\nEpisode 1: The Clown\n\nWhen the Toron
 to Fringe Festival is cancelled\, Katherine transforms her one-woman\n\ns
 how into a short film about a clown navigating the early days of lockdown
 .\n\nFeaturing: Katherine Cappellacci and Laura Cappellacci\n\n\nEpisode 
 2: Hartley & Sheel\n\n“Have you ever seen Clue?” A sketch comedy duo take
 s a crack at solving a crime in a\n\nblack-and-white murder mystery filme
 d during lockdown.\n\nFeaturing: Hartley Fanson\, Sheel Radia\, Chris Bla
 ck\, and Anthony Gullace\n\n\nEpisode 3: Respect for Actors\n\n“Our indus
 try was the first to shut down… We lost everything.” As COVID-19 brings\n
 \ntheatre and film productions to a standstill\, five actors share their 
 experiences of\n\nnavigating uncertainty\, reinventing their craft\, and 
 adapting to a rapidly changing\n\nindustry.\n\nFeaturing: Chase Jeffels\,
  Felix Beauchamp\, Noor Alimran\, Karen Scobie\, and Chelsea\n\nMuirhead\
 n\n\nEpisode 4: Phoenix Rising\n\nFaced with unprecedented challenges\, o
 ne theatre company refuses to stand still. Discover how its team adapts\,
  innovates\, and finds new ways to bring creativity to life.\n\nFeaturing
 : Brandon Nicoletti and Jordan Kenny\n\n\nEpisode 5: The Making Of\n\nGo 
 behind the scenes of The Art of Lockdown for an inside look at the creati
 ve process\, collaboration\, and work that brought this documentary serie
 s to life.\n\nFeaturing: Can Yüksel\, Felipe Gonzalez\, Brandon Nicoletti
 \, and Jordan Kenny
CATEGORIES:Film,In-Conversation,Fox-Theatre
