SUMMARY: Carson McHone: Pentimento Performance Project + Potions
DESCRIPTION:Presented with Sonic Boom\n\nIn partnership with TO Live\n\n\
 nCarson McHone: Pentimento Performance Project\n(Welland // multi-media m
 usic movement + shadow show from Daniel Romano’s Outfit folk-rocker // Me
 rge Records)\n\n\nPotions\n\n(Toronto // next-gen freak-folk supergroup)\
 n\n\nNovember 28\, 2026\n\nWavelength @ St. Anne’s\n651 Dufferin St.\n\nD
 oors 7pm\n\nAll Ages\n\n\n25 and under PWYC! (25 tickets online\, 25 tick
 ets available at the door (pending capacity - must arrive by 7:30pm to cl
 aim)\nTickets: bit.ly/PentimentoWL http://bit.ly/PentimentoWL\n\nSingle t
 ix $25 plus taxes & fees\n\n\nOn sale now!\n\n\nFind yourself on the fron
 tier of Carson McHone's imagination with The Pentimento Performance Proje
 ct. Created in collaboration with dramaturge Deana Jones and choreographe
 r Allie Blumas\, this multidisciplinary project weaves light\, shadow\, a
 nd dance into a live performance of McHone's newest album\, Pentimento.\n
 \n\nCommunity collaboration brings the project to life\, with McHone’s li
 ve performance including artists in the forefront of Canada’s folk rock a
 nd guitar scene: Daniel Romano and Tommy Major (Daniel Romano’s Outfit)\,
  Steven Lambke (Constantines)\, and composer Michael Cloud Duguay.\n\n\nT
 he evening starts with Toronto’s Potions\, a freak-folk quartet with invo
 lved and concerned lyrical stylings. Potions crafts a perfect mix for lov
 ers of the archival and the new\, the online and the analogue.\n\n\nWavel
 ength’s final monthly show of 2026 promises a tactile approach to music a
 nd movement. We invite you to come take part in this ever-forming memory!
 \n\n\nPoster by Julia Araïche and Carson McHone\n\n
CATEGORIES:Concert,Art-Show/Gallery-Event,Wavelength,St.-Anne's-Parish-Ha
 ll,Dance---Performance---Theatre
